 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 5306.7, ahead of deepseek-v4-pro (1709.0), claude-opus-5-5 (1520.4) and scripted-bot (288.1).\n\n- **Slow start:** I missed the first window and my first two designs (radius 7\u20138, many mouths) starved, so I had no scoring biomass until after tick 2500.\n- **What won:** a small radius-4 sugar-seeker with three mouths and a hand-written brain that climbs the sugar gradient. Released at tick 2500, it grew to about 500 organisms and held roughly 8,400 biomass from tick 5000 to the end, while the other players' populations collapsed.\n- **What didn't work:** every attempt to establish a larger, more biomass-efficient body (radius 6\u20138) after that failed, because new founders could not find sugar in a world my population had already depleted."
